hor_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:23:55.000151Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Prompt is in Korean but the answer drops an English paragraph in the middle. (task ref MULTI-1835)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790871885.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_67958b644e55776329b30810\", \"thread_id\": \"1790871835.000151\", \"author_id\": \"U010\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:24:45.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"A single common borrowed word seems different from an untranslated paragraph.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790871932.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_67958b644e55776329b30810\", \"thread_id\": \"1790871835.000151\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:25:32.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U011\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Did the user request one language throughout or invite code-switching? We should look at the prompt before penalizing a bilingual response.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790882060.000149\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_e22608ab9115cb70013e4e88\", \"thread_id\": \"1790882060.000149\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T19:14:20.000149Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Model mixes Spanish and English even though the user asked for Spanish.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790882117.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_e22608ab9115cb70013e4e88\", \"thread_id\": \"1790882060.000149\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T19:15:17.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"agree\", \"users\": [\"U001\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"For the specified monolingual prompt, an unexplained paragraph in another language counts against language adherence; ordinary loanwords alone do not. We should look at the prompt before penalizing a bilingual response.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790915152.000144\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_3e91ba29f70cf52ce570367f\", \"thread_id\": \"1790915152.000144\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:25:52.000144Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"It answers half in English — penalize? (task ref MULTI-5152)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790915205.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_3e91ba29f70cf52ce570367f\", \"thread_id\": \"1790915152.000144\", \"author_id\": \"U004\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:26:45.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U002\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thinking_face\", \"users\": [\"U003\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"The answer changes into English for part of the explanation; we need the prompt language to judge it. A borrowed word is not the same as shifting a whole paragraph into another language.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927651.000146\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ca3005e17eb2ae0b4b49dfc8\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927651.000146\", \"author_id\": \"U012\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:54:11.000146Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U012\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"User code-switched; should response mirror it?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927697.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ca3005e17eb2ae0b4b49dfc8\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927651.000146\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:54:57.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U012\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Because the user mixed languages, check the stated output-language requirement before penalizing a mixed-language reply; code-switching alone does not settle the score.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790935980.000148\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_75230fe43b892c1390926067\", \"thread_id\": \"1790935980.000148\", \"author_id\": \"U017\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T10:13:00.000148Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Model mixes Spanish and English even though the user asked for Spanish. (task ref MULTI-5980)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790936032.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_75230fe43b892c1390926067\", \"thread_id\": \"1790935980.000148\", \"author_id\": \"U015\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T10:13:52.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The answer stays mostly in Spanish but switches to English for the explanation.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790936079.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_75230fe43b892c1390926067\", \"thread_id\": \"1790935980.000148\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T10:14:39.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"white_check_mark\", \"users\": [\"U001\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"For the specified monolingual prompt, an unexplained paragraph in another language counts against language adherence; ordinary loanwords alone do not. We should look at the prompt before penalizing a bilingual response.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Language adherence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language adherence\\n\\n### Q: Does a single English word in a Korean or Japanese answer count as code-switching?\\nNot automatically. Ordinary loanwords are acceptable. Assess the word in context and against the required output language; an unrequested full paragraph in another language is a different issue.\\n\\n### Q: The user code-switched. Should the response mirror it?\\nCheck the explicit output-language requirement and context. User code-switching alone does not settle the score.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:0d37b1fa\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — Instructions (v1.2)\", \"sections\": [\"Language adherence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-10T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-10T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language adherence\\nFor a monolingual requirement, an unexplained paragraph in another language counts against adherence. Check the requested output language and context first. Ordinary loanwords are not automatically code-switching errors; a user mixing languages does not itself define the required output language.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_MULTI_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790861853.000153:923cb61d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"ti