 \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"expert_referral\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-12T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-12T14:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_10\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"routed\", \"outcome_status\": \"pending_expert_review\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (expert_referral; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: routed; outcome_status: pending_expert_review) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# Korean register case referred to language QA\\n\\n## Request\\nM10-KO-017 contains a polite narrative followed by a casual sentence inside quotation marks. The packet did not identify whether the quoted speaker and addressee changed.\\n\\n## TL decision\\nAlex routed the case to Hana (U008), whose recorded specialty is Korean, with the exact endings and surrounding paragraph. Do not assign a major register penalty from the ending change alone.\\n\\n## Requested assessment\\nEstablish who is speaking, whether the quote is intentional, and whether the language remains appropriate for the intended audience. The original scoring question stays open until that context is reviewed.\\n\\n## Scope\\nThis referral concerns M10-KO-017 in batch 10. It is not a general exemption for Korean register shifts.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Register and honorifics\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Register and honorifics\\n\\n### Q: Who scores Korean or Japanese register shifts?\\nRoute the case to appropriate Korean or Japanese language QA with exact sentence endings and surrounding context. Check quotations and addressee changes. The task-quality grade depends on demonstrated impact; do not assign a major penalty from the presence of a shift alone.\\n\\n### Q: Spanish tú versus usted inconsistency — major or minor?\\nAsk Spanish QA to check addressee, intended formality and discourse context. An unjustified shift can be an error, but its grade needs a case-specific rationale.\"}], \"open_review_flags\": [{\"origin\": \"agent1\", \"kind\": \"inherited_agent1_review\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_826709f4fcc9c505\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_67958b644e55776329b30810\"], \"detail\": \"Source anal